Drop the redundant protobuf runtime dep from the record_reader extension.

record_reader.cc imports google.protobuf.message_factory and
google.protobuf.descriptor_pool at runtime, so the extension needs the
protobuf Python runtime in its runfiles. The sibling data entry
:records_metadata_py_pb2 already provides it: py_proto_library attaches the
runtime declared by the registered Python proto_lang_toolchain, which in
riegeli's default configuration is this same @com_google_protobuf target.

Naming the source-built runtime explicitly bypasses toolchain resolution.
Consumers that register a Python proto toolchain whose runtime is the
protobuf wheel from PyPI end up shipping both runtimes, with import order
deciding which one loads.

--- a/python/riegeli/records/BUILD
+++ b/python/riegeli/records/BUILD
@@ -17,7 +17,6 @@ py_extension(
     data = [
         ":records_metadata_py_pb2",
         ":skipped_region",
-        "@com_google_protobuf//:protobuf_python",
     ],
     # record_reader.cc has #define before #include to influence what the
     # included files provide.
